    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1285">

                <pb facs="1240" n="1074" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1074"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115/312</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-27T16:00:00-07:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 27, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Telegram today from Chihuahua agent to American S. and R. Company office here
                    that authorities there have assessed company five thousand pesos as part of
                    forced loan to pay troops, also expressing belief that train service between
                    Chihuahua and Juarez would be resumed immediately. See my June 26, 4 p.m.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d1285-f1"/> and June 27, noon.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1285-f2"
                    /> Confirmatory information from others of forced loan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cobb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
